    "reply": "A search for BRCA1 genetic data retrieved a set of SequenceVariant records [1][2]. These records only partly answer the question because they provide variant names but omit functional interpretations [3][4]. The provided records lack information on variant classification evidence or genomic assembly context [5][6].\n\n## Identified Sequence Variants\nThe findings consist of structural identifiers linked to a specific reference transcript [7][8]. The first record is SequenceVariant ClinVar:1000183, name: NM_007294.4(BRCA1):c.4709T>C (p.Leu1570Pro) [1]. Another finding is SequenceVariant ClinVar:1000551, name: NM_007294.4(BRCA1):c.3664G>A (p.Glu1222Lys) [2]. A further entry is SequenceVariant record ClinVar:1010631 [29].\n\n## Evidence and Assembly Data\nThe records catalog specific missense alterations rather than providing classification evidence [9][10]. For instance, one record is SequenceVariant ClinVar:1005082, name: NM_007294.4(BRCA1):c.1930T>G (p.Cys644Gly) [11]. An additional result is SequenceVariant ClinVar:1005528, name: NM_007294.4(BRCA1):c.4685C>G (p.Pro1562Arg) [12]. I could not find information on the classification evidence or assembly context for these variants [13][14].",
